
Usage: /ENTER <chan-name>
  This  command  allows  you  to  change  from  the current channel to
  another  one.   Note  that entering the channel you specified is not
  always  possible  since some channels have restrictions such as user
  limits.   If the environment variable CHANNELLINGER is set to Y, you
  will  not exit the current channel, you must explicitly use /exit to
  do  so.   When  CHANNELLINGER is Y you can be in several channels at
  once, but only one can be current at a time.

  Example:
     /ENTER amiga

  See Also:
     /EXIT
     /SETENV CHANNELLINGER

